Subject: question about trait-dependent dispersal
Message-ID: <oKjZEec9xJk.Z8e8l5gLAwAJ@biogeobears.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/biogeobears/c/oKjZEec9xJk/m/Z8e8l5gLAwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi everyone

I would like to apply the biogeography models that account for trait-based dispersal using the model described in (Klaus and Matzke 2020). In my data I have a phylogeny of ~150 taxa and five areas, and one binary character (ground and arboreal), and I would like to test if the dispersal rates are different between arboreal and ground spiders. Thus, I would like to ask if anyone have some code or tutorial about how to run this analysis?

I have run the code provided in the supplementary of the article named "fast example". However, this code does not have the option to plot the results of both the reconstruction of the biogeographic areas and the binary character. In addition, the code does not provide the function for model testing using AIC. Although I have done model testing and plotting the results using biogeobears before, I have never done it with the trait dispersal model and I want to make sure that I am doing it correctly. Thus, I would like to ask if anyone have some code that includes these functions?

best regards and thanks in advance for any help

Nicolas

